{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#774","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#774","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#774\",\"parent_revision\":\"8964194dde9a3b14963995991912ba6fe4db302a\",\"root_revision\":\"77c4d4c2414d2c93179d95479470af34c9e3d7389ca2b46eb4e8d37bd7b0a156\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSKILL.md files across the repo contain `Agent(subagent_type=\\\"...\\\", prompt=\\\"...\\\")` call templates as instructions for how to delegate. This is wrong for three reasons:\\n\\n1. Redundant \u2014 the orchestrator already has the Agent tool schema in its system prompt every session\\n2. Fragile \u2014 when the API changes (Task\u2192Agent rename, parameter names), every file goes stale. This already happened twice: Task\u2192Agent rename (30+ files stale) and hallucinated `agent=` parameter (18 files, 39+ occurrences)\\n3. Contradicts delegation-format.md \u2014 the existing rule in `.claude/rules/delegation-format.md` explicitly says \\\"This is Tool API syntax. Workflow documentation is not code\\\" and lists `Agent(...)` call templates as a Wrong Format\\n\\nThe correct convention per delegation-format.md is prose delegation steps:\\n```\\nN. Task is [description] with subagent_type=\\\"plugin:agent-name\\\"\\n   Context to include in the prompt: [specific file paths]\\n   Output: [specific artifact the agent produces]\\n```\\n\\nScope: ~50 files across plugins/, workshops/, .claude/knowledge/, .claude/plan/ contain `Agent(subagent_type=` call template syntax that needs converting to the delegation format standard.\\n\\nSuccess: zero `Agent(subagent_type=` call templates remain in SKILL.md or reference files. All delegation instructions use the prose format from delegation-format.md.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-17T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **replace agent(...) call templates in skills with delegation format standard** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-17T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 discovered during Task\u2192Agent rename audit (2026-03-17)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-17\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Goal**: Zero `Agent(subagent_type=` call templates remain in SKILL.md and reference files; all delegation instructions use the prose format from `.claude/rules/delegation-format.md`.\\n\\n**Conditions**:\\n\\n1. Correct target format is defined | AVAILABLE \u2014 `.claude/rules/delegation-format.md` specifies the prose step format exactly\\n2. Files requiring change are enumerable | AVAILABLE \u2014 grep `Agent\\\\(subagent_type=` across repo returns deterministic results\\n3. Exclusions from fix scope are identifiable | DERIVABLE \u2014 files in `.claude/rules/` (canonical wrong-format example) and `research/` (notes) are not instructional SKILL.md/reference content\\n4. No downstream consumers depend on the call template syntax | DERIVABLE \u2014 these are doc strings read by AI agents at runtime; changing to prose format produces equivalent delegation behaviour\\n5. Validation command exists | AVAILABLE \u2014 same grep used to find matches is the zero-state verification\\n\\n**Decision**: APPROVED\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Technical debt with recurrence risk. The Task\u2192Agent rename already stalened 30+ files. Every new API change will stale these files again. Fixing now prevents the next round of stale content.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Nothing blocked on this item\\n- Bottleneck: Each API rename propagates to every SKILL.md containing call templates \u2014 multiplying maintenance cost linearly with file count\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n**Verified file count (2026-03-30 grep)**: 14 files total, 35 occurrences.\\n\\nFiles requiring change (11 files, ~32 occurrences):\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md` \u2014 8 occurrences\\n- `plugins/holistic-linting/skills/holistic-linting-orchestrator/SKILL.md` \u2014 5 occurrences\\n- `plugins/process-siren/skills/woo-sailor/SKILL.md` \u2014 4 occurrences\\n- `plugins/python3-development/skills/specialist-skill-routing/SKILL.md` \u2014 4 occurrences\\n- `plugins/python3-development/skills/stinkysnake/SKILL.md` \u2014 3 occurrences\\n- `plugins/holistic-linting/skills/holistic-linting/SKILL.md` \u2014 3 occurrences\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-agent-lifecycle/SKILL.md` \u2014 1 occurrence\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-agent-lifecycle/references/agent-lifecycle-audit.md` \u2014 1 occurrence\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/docs/ERROR_CODES.md` \u2014 1 occurrence\\n- `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/skills/orchestrator-discipline/references/investigation-escalation.md` \u2014 1 occurrence\\n- `.claude/knowledge/workflow-diagrams/asset-decision-tree.md` \u2014 1 occurrence\\n\\nExcluded (intentional or notes, not instructional):\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/delegation-format.md` \u2014 1 occurrence, canonical wrong-format example, MUST NOT change\\n- `research/research-agent-patterns/github-patterns.md` \u2014 1 occurrence, research notes\\n- `.claude/skills/daily-releases/notes/ai-analysis-subagent-fix.md` \u2014 1 occurrence, session note\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates recurrence: prose format is API-agnostic; future renames do not stale docs\\n- Reduces contradiction: SKILL.md files no longer contradict the rule in `.claude/rules/delegation-format.md`\\n- Reduces context noise: orchestrators reading skill files no longer encounter redundant tool-call syntax they already know from system prompt\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nEvery delegation instruction in SKILL.md and reference files uses the prose form:\\n\\n```text\\nN. Task is [description] with subagent_type='plugin:agent-name'\\n   Context to include in the prompt: [specific file paths]\\n   Output: [specific artifact]\\n```\\n\\nThe pattern `Agent(subagent_type=` does not appear in any SKILL.md or reference file. It appears only in `.claude/rules/delegation-format.md` as a labelled wrong-format example.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -r 'Agent(subagent_type=' plugins/ .claude/knowledge/ .claude/plan/ workshops/` returns zero matches\\n2. `.claude/rules/delegation-format.md` still contains the pattern exactly once (the wrong-format example \u2014 must not be removed)\\n3. Each converted file has delegation steps in prose format with `subagent_type=`, `Context to include in the prompt:`, and `Output:` fields\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Rule | /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/delegation-format.md |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md (8 occurrences \u2014 highest density) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/holistic-linting/skills/holistic-linting-orchestrator/SKILL.md (5 occurrences) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/process-siren/skills/woo-sailor/SKILL.md (4 occurrences) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/python3-development/skills/specialist-skill-routing/SKILL.md (4 occurrences) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None \u2014 this is cleanup; no downstream items wait on it\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 11 files, mechanical text replacement per file. Each file requires reading context around each occurrence to write an accurate prose replacement (subagent_type + context + output). No logic changes. Linting pass required after each file edit (`uv run prek run --files <file>`).\\n\",\"digest\":\"638bd1d3c0efe12fc770326fe464667898fd2